1.4.1 The while Statement
A while statement repeatedly executes a section of code so long as a given con-
dition is true. W e can use a while to write a program to sum the numbers from 1
through 10 inclusive as follows:
#include <iostream>
int main()
{
int sum = 0, val = 1;
// keep executing the while as long as val is less than or equal to 10
while (val <= 10) {
sum += val; // assigns sum + val to sum
++val; // add 1 to val
}
std::cout << "Sum of 1 to 10 inclusive is "
<< sum << std::endl;
return 0;
}
